* t99delopen.a -- CONF68K test t99: a file that is open cannot be deleted.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): "The caller must have non-sharable write access to* the file (the file may not already be open) or an error results"* (I$Delete, page 2 - 7). The page's error list names only E$BPNam, and* which code an open file earns is not stated, so the test asks that the* delete is REFUSED and does not say with what.** t30 is the two-process form of this -- one process deletes what another* holds open, and reports E$Share. This is the single-process form, which* needs no handshake and no second device, and which a host filesystem is* likely to answer differently: unlinking an open file is ordinary on Unix.** obs is 100 if the delete is refused while the path is open, plus 10 if it* succeeds once the path is closed, plus 1 if the file is then really gone* (a reopen reports E$PNNF, 216): 111.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1ICreate set $83IOpen set $84IClose set $8FIDelete set $87ATTRS set $001BEPNNF set 216*EXPECT set 111* psect t99delopen,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 trap #0 dc.w IDelete lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 move.w #ATTRS,d1 clr.l d2 trap #0 dc.w ICreate bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d7 moveq #0,d6** open, and therefore undeletable lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 trap #0 dc.w IDelete bcc.s t99shut addi.l #100,d6*t99shut moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IClose** closed, and therefore deletable lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 trap #0 dc.w IDelete bcs.s t99gone addi.l #10,d6** and really gone: asked even when the delete above failed, because each* digit here stands on its own -- a skipped check reads as a failed one* and sent the first draft of this test looking for a caching bug.t99gone lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #1,d0 trap #0 dc.w IOpen bcc.s t99open cmpi.w #EPNNF,d1 bne.s t99v addq.l #1,d6 bra.s t99vt99open move.w d0,d7 moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w ICloset99v cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*fname dc.b "SCRATCH/t99.dat",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t99 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  a file that is open cannot be deleted",0 ends